900 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 398 0 R
/T (Hedging instruments are financial tools used to mitigate the risks associated with foreign exchange fluctuations. These instruments help stabilize cash flows, protect profit margins, and ensure predictable financial performance amid currency volatility. By employing hedging instruments such as forward contracts, currency options, swaps, and futures, the company can effectively manage its exposure to foreign currencies resulting from international operations, transactions, and investments. This approach supports strategic planning and enhances the company's competitiveness in the global market.)
/E (Hedging instruments are financial tools used to mitigate the risks associated with foreign exchange fluctuations. These instruments help stabilize cash flows, protect profit margins, and ensure predictable financial performance amid currency volatility. By employing hedging instruments such as forward contracts, currency options, swaps, and futures, the company can effectively manage its exposure to foreign currencies resulting from international operations, transactions, and investments. This approach supports strategic planning and enhances the company's competitiveness in the global market.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [33]
>>
